# Sprinting is land only (docs/design/sprinting.md Phase B, section 4). It ends
# when the player boards the raft and cannot start on the deck or at the helm.
# (Boarding itself is covered by a unit test in walk.rs: `stand` teleports,
# which resets the player's sprint, so no script can show a sprint ending.)
# The mouse turns the player round (to face south, away from the helm cell,
# which would end a sprint by a head-on hit) so only the deck rule can end it.

case a double-tap on the deck does not start a sprint
start walk raft
click
lock
stand deck
mouse 1257 0
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x4
expect sprinting = false

case a double-tap at the helm does not start a sprint
start walk raft
click
lock
stand helm
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x4
expect sprinting = false

case sprinting on the islet still works
start walk raft
click
lock
stand planter
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x2
expect sprinting = true

case sprinting on the runway still works
start walk raft
click
lock
runway 12
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x4
expect sprinting = true
